Summary: Install placeholder AMD and NVIDIA DLLs in 64-bit prefixes, for D3DMetal and DXMT
Category: graphics
Kind: feature
Origin: crossover
  Version: 26.3.0
  CW-Hacks: 22435
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz
  Files: loader/wine.inf.in
  Changes: CX 26.3.0's lines without atidxx64.dll, which only D3DMetal ships
  Note: the wine.inf part of CW HACK 22435; the winemac.drv part is
    winemac-export-macdrv-functions. Sikarugir 10.0_8 ships it: its
    share/wine/wine.inf has CX's three lines with CX's comment; it is the only
    difference in share/
Upstream: no
Why: Have wineboot put placeholder nvapi64.dll and nvngx.dll in a 64-bit
 prefix's system32. No builtin DLLs have those names, so setupapi writes
 generic placeholder DLLs. Outside prefix setup, Wine loads a builtin DLL
 only if a file of that name is in the prefix (find_builtin_without_file in
 dlls/ntdll/loader.c); with a placeholder in system32, DXMT's nvapi64.dll and
 nvngx.dll on its DLL path (WINEDLLPATH_DXMT) can be loaded. Without a
 renderer path supplying them, loading these names fails with error 126 as
 before (shown on 11.22 build0); programs can only see that the files exist.
 The 10.0 copy also adds atidxx64.dll, for D3DMetal, which this build
 doesn't support on Wine 11.x.
Programs: none known
Enable: by WINEDLLPATH_DXMT (ntdll-renderer-dll-paths) supplying DXMT's nvapi64.dll and nvngx.dll; the files are in every 64-bit prefix
Related: ntdll-renderer-dll-paths, winemetal-stub
Status: 11.21, 11.22: 2026-11-26: atidxx64.dll dropped (D3DMetal can't run on
 11.x)
 11.21: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T005336 and T023339 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed
 11.22: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T002454 and T025644 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed

